<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE D2. The `kie` FLAVOR's decisionService shape, and the SOLE justification
  for DmnFlavor existing at all: a decision that carries
  <knowledgeRequirement><requiredKnowledge href="#svc"/> and INVOKES the service
  from FEEL.

      decisionService `bundle` = { output: total, encapsulated: step, input: n }
      decision `via_bundle` = bundle(n: n + 100)      <<< KR to the SERVICE

  Section 13.4 calls this "the one measurement that is not allowed to be
  inherited". Committing it as a fixture is precisely how it stops being
  inherited: the claim now re-runs on every CI job instead of being copied
  forward in prose.

  The argument is `n + 100`, not `n`, so the service call cannot accidentally
  agree with the plain top-level evaluation of `total` under the same context.
  Without that the two would coincide and a service that silently did nothing
  would look like a service that worked.

  KIE   : passes; the caller's value is correct.
  Camunda 8 : parse() throws
      java.lang.ClassCastException: class ...DecisionServiceImpl cannot be cast
      to class ...BusinessKnowledgeModel
  and takes the WHOLE FILE with it, not just the calling decision. Wired
  HarnessMustFail on the Camunda leg for that reason.

  UPGRADE TRIPWIRE, same as spouse-context-table.dmn carries. If the Camunda leg
  ever starts PASSING, zeebe-dmn has learned to invoke a decisionService, the
  `camunda` flavor's reason to exist has evaporated, and DmnFlavor should be
  deleted rather than maintained. A green day on a HarnessMustFail fixture is
  the signal to go read the release notes, not to relax the assertion.

  D3 (svc-invoked-minus-kr.dmn) is this file MINUS the one knowledgeRequirement
  element, and is what isolates the cause to that element rather than to
  anything else in the file.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31, reproducing section 13.4 exactly:
    KIE 8.44  : validator and build clean; 6/6 values; via_bundle = 209 and 201,
                i.e. the service really ran on the substituted argument.
    Camunda 8 : PARSE INVALID, whole file:
                  class org.camunda.bpm.model.dmn.impl.instance.DecisionServiceImpl
                  cannot be cast to class
                  org.camunda.bpm.model.dmn.instance.BusinessKnowledgeModel
                0 decisions parsed. Not a per-decision failure, a per-FILE one.

-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_svc_invoked" name="svc_invoked" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/svc_invoked" exporter="hand">
  <inputData id="input_n" name="n">
    <variable id="input_n_var" name="n" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_step" name="step">
    <variable id="decision_step_var" name="step" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_step_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_step_lit">
      <text>n * 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_total" name="total">
    <variable id="decision_total_var" name="total" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_total_step">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_step"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_total_lit">
      <text>step + 1</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decisionService id="svc_bundle" name="bundle">
    <variable id="svc_bundle_var" name="bundle" typeRef="number"/>
    <outputDecision href="#decision_total"/>
    <encapsulatedDecision href="#decision_step"/>
    <inputData href="#input_n"/>
  </decisionService>
  <decision id="decision_via_bundle" name="via_bundle">
    <variable id="decision_via_bundle_var" name="via_bundle" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_via_bundle_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <knowledgeRequirement id="kr_via_bundle">
      <requiredKnowledge href="#svc_bundle"/>
    </knowledgeRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_via_bundle_lit">
      <text>bundle(n: n + 100)</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
</definitions>
